Chapter: SpikeTruckMain
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Safari chapter Sky
  cites Poc chapter Spike
  cites Poc chapter SpikePrint

 SPIKE ONLY. THROWAWAY. The two truck stills, and a SECOND ENTRY rather than two
 more lines in SpikeMain, for one reason: THE BUMP HEAP.

 The transpiled prelude bump-allocates and never reclaims (PORTING_NOTES C6), and
 the wasm shim's per-frame arena rewind (C8) is a thing the SHIM does -- a native
 spike binary has no shim and no rewind, so one process pays for every frame it
 prints, for the whole run. Six viewpoints came to within a rounding error of the
 4 GiB reserve; adding a seventh exhausted it and the binary aborted with

     cx heap: exhausted at 4294965457 + 7000 of 4294967296

 which is a page-perfect illustration of C6 and not a bug in anything. A second
 process starts with a fresh 4 GiB, so the fix is a second entry and one more line
 in harness/spike.sh. It is also the cheapest fix available: raising the reserve
 would make the RUN cost real memory rather than address space, on a two-core box.

 The printing is `Poc chapter SpikePrint`, cited rather than restated, so the two
 binaries emit the same format and spike_svg.py reads them concatenated without
 knowing there were two. It is a chapter rather than a cite of SpikeMain because a
 bundle is one flat namespace and two `opening`s collide -- B5, found by trying it.

 We say:

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (scene-line "truck-day" u-truck-day)
    print-line-uni (all-cmds (spike-frame-near u-truck-day spike-truck-lead) 0)
    print-line-uni (scene-line "truck-dusk" u-truck-dusk)
    print-line-uni (all-cmds (spike-frame-near u-truck-dusk spike-truck-lead) 0)
  end
